      ],
      "executable_checks": [
        "Integration test: Submit a block via P2P with base_fee_per_gas off by 1 wei and verify it is rejected as InvalidBlock",
        "Integration test: Verify parent_gas_limit used in gas target calculation comes from chain state, not from the proposed block's header fields",
        "Convergence test: Simulate 100 blocks with gas_used at various percentages of gas_limit and verify base fee follows the EIP-1559 convergence curve with elasticity = 2",
        "Fuzz test: Fuzz parent_gas_limit, parent_gas_used, and parent_base_fee_per_gas inputs to calculate_base_fee_per_gas and verify output matches the specification formula"
      ],
      "notes": "Source: PROP-0072, Supporting node check for actor-block-proposer and actor-evm. The block proposer is an external actor communicating across trust boundary tb-012. The EVM (actor-evm) processes the base fee internally. This check verifies that the internal logic supporting boundary security correctly derives the gas target from immutable parent state, preventing a proposer from influencing the target computation."
    }
